- fresh restricted and upgraded Codex continuation;
- restricted native rejection with zero native compact calls;
- upgraded native-decline behavior;
- restart durability with one persisted compaction/latch and no repeat;
- substituted and revoked writers rejected before provider I/O, native requests,
  or transcript commits;
- exact execution refs, checksummed artifacts, auth/Windows fail-closed
  contracts, producer tests, real systemd recovery, and `check:changed`.

The task-owned proof lease was released after artifact verification. Run 697 and
proof from superseded heads were not reused.
